<section id="structure-base">
   	 	<section>
			<h1>Website structure and navigation</h1>
		</section>
   	 	<section>
			<h2>Page title</h2>
			<p>Unique and meaningful</p>
			<pre data-trim><code is:raw>&lt;title&gt;page name | website name&lt;/title&gt;</code></pre>
			<pre data-trim><code is:raw>&lt;title&gt;contact | STIB&lt;/title&gt;</code></pre>
			<p>Configure your CMS to do this automatically</p>
			<aside class="notes"></aside>
		</section>	
		<section>
			<h2>Why?</h2>
			<ul>
				<li>First thing read by screenreader</li>
			    <li>Search results</li>
				<li>Favourites</li>
				<li>Tabs </li>
			</ul>
			<aside class="notes">The title will help a screenreader user know on whch page they are, without having to read the page. The title can also be useful to switch to a different browser tab for a person using voice recognition. </aside>
		</section>	

		<section>
<h2>Multiple ways</h2>
<ul>
<li>More than one way to locate a webpage within a set of webpages, for example:
<ul>
 	<li>search function</li>
 	<li>sitemap</li>
 </ul> </li>
<li>except where the webpage is the result of, or a step in, a process</li>
</ul>
</section>
	
<section>
<h2>Consistent navigation</h2>
<p>Navigational mechanisms that are repeated on multiple web pages within a set of web pages occur in the same relative order each time they are repeated, unless a change is initiated by the user.</p>
</section>
	
<section>
<h2>Consistent identification</h2>
<p>Components that have the same functionality within a set of web pages are identified consistently.</p>
</section>		

<section>
<h2>Example</h2>
<pre><code is:raw>&lt;p&gt;You have to register...&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;a href="#"&gt;Register&lt;/a&gt;
</code></pre>
</section>
   	 	
